  "levelOverridesDescription": "Black level and range above black for cameras LibRaw reads wrongly; always applied, independent of the base exposure setting. Key: normalized maker|model, optionally |ISO (the ISO entry wins and applies only at that ISO). black -1 keeps LibRaw's black level, black -2 measures it per file from the masked sensor border, black -3 reads black and white from Canon's ColorData of the file at the words given under colorData (falling back to the border). range is passed to LibRaw as user_sat, which LibRaw applies after black subtraction; instead of range an entry may give the raw white level (white), and the range is then white minus black. librawBlack and librawRange record what LibRaw reported for the measured file and are not read.",
  "canonColorDataLayouts": {
    "7|1251": 715,
    "7|1337": 715,
    "7|1338": 715,
    "9|1346": 719,
